The greatness of a man's power is the measure of his surrender=2E
<br>
Nothing which has entered into our experience is ever lost=2E
<br>
What is fame? The advantage of being known by people of whom you yoursel=
f know nothing, and for whom you care as little=2E
<br>
Begin somewhere: you cannot build a reputation on what you intend to do=2E=

<br>
No wind is of service to him that is bound for nowhere=2E
<br>
Be gentle to all, and stern with yourself=2E
<br>
Life is nothing without friendship=2E
<br>
A man is too apt to forget that in this world he cannot have everything=2E=
 A choice is all that is left him=2E
<br>
Liberty consists in wholesome restraint=2E
<br>
When soldiers have been baptized in the fire of a battle-field, they hav=
e all one rank in my eyes=2E
<br>
In business for yourself, not by yourself=2E
<br>
Good things, when short, are twice as good=2E
<br>
